WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:05.171
-You guys, as you know,
today is Thanksgiving.

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.773
And I'm always thankful
for my writers.

00:00:06.773 --> 00:00:08.875
They write hundreds --
This is true.

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:10.409
They write hundreds
of jokes every day

00:00:10.409 --> 00:00:12.711
just to get the 10 or 12
we use in the monologue.

00:00:12.711 --> 00:00:15.048
And let's face it -- a lot of
those jokes aren't great.

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:18.117
And, honestly, sometimes, I
think they just throw in

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:20.620
some real stinkers
just to fill up a page

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.356
and meet the assignment,
which is totally understandable.

00:00:24.356 --> 00:00:26.258
But just because the holidays
are here doesn't mean

00:00:26.258 --> 00:00:28.661
we can get lazy,
which means it's time for a

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.296
"Surprise Inspection."

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.298
[ Fanfare ]

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:40.340
Apologies for the neighborhood
dog that's probably barking

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.309
after that opening package.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:44.710
So, here's how this works.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:47.113
These are real jokes
that were actually submitted by

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:49.516
my writers that are
unusable for the show.

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:51.618
Some are dumb,
some are patently offensive,

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:54.754
and some are just baffling.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.089
And, more importantly,
the writers don't know

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:57.891
we're doing this,
and because a lot of them

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:00.927
don't watch the show, they'll
never know we're doing this.

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:03.195
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:04.631
So let's get to it.

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:07.766
The FBI reportedly searched
the site of a former landfill

00:01:07.766 --> 00:01:09.068
in New Jersey last month,

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:11.304
looking for the body of
union leader Jimmy Hoffa.

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.806
To give you an idea how long
they've been searching for him,

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:15.809
watch "The Irishman."

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:21.914
According to a new study,

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:24.651
ricotta is
the healthiest cheese,

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:27.687
but, still, you "cannoli"
have so much.

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:29.722
[ Audience groans ]

00:01:31.523 --> 00:01:34.194
Uh, Ian wrote that. Here's Ian.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.765
Looks like a nice guy, but now,
you know, if you see him,

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:42.568
hopefully you'll go
the other way.

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:45.104
West Virginia senator
Joe Manchin is reportedly

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:46.405
in talks for a book deal.

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:49.308
The book will be sold at
Barnes &amp; Ignoble.

00:01:49.308 --> 00:01:51.344
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:56.349
I mean, can you imagine sitting
and writing a joke where

00:01:56.349 --> 00:02:00.086
the punch line is "Ignoble"?

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.924
'Cause we don't even
hear it right.

00:02:05.924 --> 00:02:07.093
That was written by Matt.

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:08.828
There he is.

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:15.668
I mean, that's the haircut of a
guy who isn't reading the room.

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:17.704
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.307
Today -- Oh, boy, this one.

00:02:22.307 --> 00:02:24.444
Today was
National Louisiana Day.

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:27.079
Uh-oh! I forgot to
"bayou" something.

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:29.115
[ Audience groans ]

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:32.452
Take a look at Bryan. Yeah.

00:02:35.388 --> 00:02:38.691
According to a new survey,
nearly 25% of Americans believe

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:42.228
or are unsure if the coronavirus
vaccine contains a microchip.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:44.931
The only way to find a microchip
is to turn the bag upside down

00:02:44.931 --> 00:02:47.000
and pour it directly
into your mouth.

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:52.438
Here's the most shocking --

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:55.240
There's something truly shocking
about that joke.

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:58.143
At the bottom of each of these,
I have asked our head writer,

00:02:58.143 --> 00:03:00.180
Alex Baze,
to write who wrote them.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.916
so that I can,
you know, shame them.

00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:08.254
The bottom of this card,
it says, "Karen and Ian."

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:10.290
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.629
It was a collaboration.

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:21.834
To get that joke,
we had to pay two salaries.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.870
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.907
"Uh, microchip, something small.

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:30.042
Where do they have small chips?
Oh, I don't know."

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:31.243
"Uh, tiny poker chips!"

00:03:31.243 --> 00:03:32.978
No! There's got to be
something better, Karen!"

00:03:32.978 --> 00:03:34.547
"We can do this, Ian!"

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:37.417
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:40.953
I don't know if we're gonna
keep all these in,

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:42.421
so let me just say,
if you're watching at home

00:03:42.421 --> 00:03:45.624
and, at some moment, it went to
a full frame that said like,

00:03:45.624 --> 00:03:48.461
"Surprise Inspection,"
that means we cut one.

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:50.496
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:53.866
Alright, well,
maybe the same Scollins.

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.535
We'll keep Scollins up.
He wrote another one.

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:57.269
And, obviously, he's probably --

00:03:57.269 --> 00:03:59.037
When he watches this,
he'll feel terrible about

00:03:59.037 --> 00:04:02.542
ruining Thanksgiving with that
Michael Jackson joke.

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:04.276
And he'll say, "Hopefully Baze
put in another one

00:04:04.276 --> 00:04:05.645
that will win everybody back."

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:07.313
Today was National Sardines Day,

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.315
so maybe the wife will
let you do it in the can.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:10.783
Nope.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.230
Britain's Prince William,
yesterday,

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:26.399
attended the
Tusk Conservation Awards

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:28.501
to honor
wildlife-protections workers

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:31.437
and also because he's
an endangered bald regal.

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:33.473
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:39.545
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:41.314
This has -- Tanks for nothin'.

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:43.683
This has been
"Surprise Inspection."

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:45.685
[ Fanfare ]

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:47.687
[ Cheers and applause ]

